  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Paraguay Floods 2014</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An estimated 201 800were affected by heavy rainfall and flooding. 98% of the 70 000 displaced are in Asunci&#xf3;n. Most affected areas include Alto Paraguay Presidente Hayes (Bajo Chaco) Asunci&#xf3;n and &#xd1;eembuc&#xfa;. This ten-month emergency operation led by the Paraguayan Red Cross enabled the National Society to provide 2 765 people with psychosocial support; 7 030 people with basic hygiene promotion activities and information; 2 685 families who were located in collective centres were provided with hygiene kits kitchen kits tarpaulins and toolkits to cover and protect the roofs and walls of their shelters. The PRC also provided 386 families with buckets water dispensing bags and jerry cans from the standard Federation Kit 2 for water and sanitation disaster response. Additionally another 1 998 families received supplies for the transport and storage of safe water consumption (buckets and water filters). A total of 345 families received supplies for water treatment (water purification supplies and tablets for water treatment). The Paraguayan Red Cross also distributed food kits to 1 370 families.</narrative>
  </description>
